  "title": "The Chinese room thought experiment",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "1b05e98d-c4d2-49ec-8de8-04159761c736",
      "text": "A person who knows no Chinese is locked in a room with batches of Chinese symbols and rules in English for matching them by shape. The outsiders call the batches a script, a story and questions, the person’s output answers, and the rules the program. With practice the answers become indistinguishable from those of native speakers.",
